From: YanIanZ <iwayanbagusaryadarma@student.telkomuniversity.ac.id>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 02:03:36 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] SourbyCraft - consume rejected network frames

Channel close invokes decodeLast. Consume explicitly rejected input so
the same frame cannot be counted again during shutdown.

diff --git a/net/minecraft/network/PacketDecoder.java b/net/minecraft/network/PacketDecoder.java
index 8339257434e13b1b7bb68cd8019a13b877e63a29..72e3307725b03eda7143860c8096dc3bc516c96d 100644
--- a/net/minecraft/network/PacketDecoder.java
+++ b/net/minecraft/network/PacketDecoder.java
@@ -78,6 +78,10 @@ public class PacketDecoder<T extends PacketListener> extends ByteToMessageDecode
         }
 
         ProtocolSwapHandler.handleInboundTerminalPacket(ctx, packet);
+        } catch (dev.iyanz.sourbycraft.security.SecurityGuards.Rejected rejected) {
+            // SourbyCraft - closing the channel calls decodeLast; do not replay a rejected frame.
+            input.skipBytes(input.readableBytes());
+            throw rejected;
         } // SourbyCraft - clear the scope even when codecs or explicit KICK guards throw
     }
 }
